[Term]
id: PROMOT:0032014
name: Debilidad fatigable muscular axial
def: "A type of weakness of the axial muscles (i.e., of the muscles of the head and neck, spine, and ribs) that occurs after a muscle group is used and lessens if the muscle group has some rest. That is, there is diminution of the strength of the axial muscles with repetitive muscle actions." [] {IAO:0000119="HP:0003473"}
